<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="034" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>External-plane message send endpoint — thread post, no email (FR-11)</title>
    <phase>3 BFF features</phase>
    <gate>after 030 and 033</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New external write endpoint with Tier-2 check on send (tags bff-api, auth)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Write path on shared Communication pipeline; authorization-critical</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>extends ExternalMessageEndpoints.cs created by 033; touches shared Services/Communication</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030, 033</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, testing, regarding</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add POST /api/v1/external/{root}/{id}/messages that posts a message to the record's thread as the caller, without sending any email, and only on records the caller can access.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. ASP.NET Core developer familiar with the Spaarke communication pipeline. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>The send route creates one sprk_communication regarding the record (ADR-024 regarding fields set the same way CommunicationService does), stamped with the caller (task-030 method), with no Graph send and no OBO; outside-set records return 403.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner 2026-10-08: thread post + notify members, no outbound email, no attachments. CommunicationService.SendAsync (:1107) sends via Graph (OBO /me/sendMail on the user path, shared mailbox on the app-only path); CIAM contacts and Model 1 guests have no usable mailbox (#1464). CommunicationService.cs:1022 notes app-only ownership of Direct-thread messages — look for an existing app-only 'post to thread' path to extend. Member notification is wired in task 036 (email) and appears automatically in the task-037 feed.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalMessageEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter.cs</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalMessageSendTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Every route this task adds or modifies is mapped inside the /api/v1/external group (Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:60-63) so it inherits the ExternalCollaboration policy and CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter. No route in this task is mapped outside that group.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No OBO on the external plane: every Dataverse and SPE call this task adds is app-only and scoped to the caller's accessible set (spec NFR-01).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">State the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md). Measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build: more than +5 MB needs written justification; the total must stay at or under 60 MB. No new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build only on the net10 SDK (10.0.1xx). Run /conflict-check before opening the PR: Api/ExternalAccess/** and Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** are shared with unified-access-control-r2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Extend CommunicationService with (or reuse) an app-only thread-post method that creates the sprk_communication row without calling Graph; never fork the pipeline and never call /me/sendMail.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The record must be in the caller's accessible set (service requests: requester scope); checked before any write, fail-closed. The sender is the resolved principal; any sender/from/createdby in the body is ignored.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Body only (plain text, max length enforced, e.g. 10,000 chars); attachments are rejected (400). The message is not internal-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Coordinate with open PR #1494 (Services/Communication) via /conflict-check before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>external message send</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
