      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files listed above, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Read CommunicationService (SendAsync, RegardingLookupMap, the Direct-thread app-only branch near :1022) and CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter.</step>
    <step order="2">Add or reuse the app-only thread-post method; it sets regarding via the existing map and the sender via the task-030 stamp.</step>
    <step order="3">Map POST in ExternalMessageEndpoints.cs with request validation (body required, length cap, no attachments).</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: accessible record → 201 and the row appears in the task-033 read; outside the set → 403 and no row; sender equals caller even when the body names someone else; no Graph client call is made; attachments → 400; own service request → 201; another's service request → 403.</step>
    <step order="5">Seeding proof on the Tier-2 check: bypass it, confirm the outside-set test fails, restore.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (0 errors) and `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` (all pass); measure publish size per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md and record it in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/notes/task-034-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If posting a thread message without a Graph send breaks an invariant elsewhere (e.g. communications assumed to have a message id or mailbox), STOP and escalate with the dependents found.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>CommunicationService.SendAsync (:1107) sends mail; no external-plane entry point exists.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the pipeline (regarding map, row shape) — extended in place; the route itself is new because the external plane needs its own Tier-2 check and principal stamping.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A granted user cannot send a message on a record or answer a question on their service request (G6).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalMessageEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalMessageSendTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A send on an accessible record returns 201 and the message appears in that record's thread (task-033 read).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A send on a record outside the caller's set returns 403 and creates no row.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The stored sender is the caller (systemuser → sprk_createdbyperson, contact → sprk_createdbycontact) even if the request names another sender.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No email is sent and no Graph mail API is called.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A request with attachments returns 400; an empty or over-long body returns 400.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The requester can post on their own service request; another caller gets 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seeding proof is recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build is green; all unit tests pass; publish size is recorded and at or under 60 MB with no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative and edge cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-11. Member email notification: task 036.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting this task, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow the task-execute skill for the mandatory pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
